WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.710
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:07.430
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.070
So far on Aikatsu!

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:16.150
I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo, a third-year middle school student at the idol school Starlight Academy. {I feel like I do this differently every time}

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.950
We all use Aikatsu cards to do our idol activities.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.920
There's a new idol school called Dream Academy, or DreAca for short.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.170
One of the students there, Otoshiro Seira-chan,

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:31.800
as well as her producer Saegusa Kii-chan, who recently made her idol debut, are both amazing.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.390
My Aikatsu getting more and more passionate!

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.070
Ah, it's here!

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.270
What's here?

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.640
DreAca's Aikatsu online magazine.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.440
I subscribed so I could keep up on the latest news.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.290
Starli's KiriAo is reading DreAca's AiMag!

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.400
You don't need to shorten "Starlight" or "Kiriya Aoi".

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:57.780
What's up?

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:04.410
It says that DreAca's Otoshiro Seira-chan and Saegusa Kii-chan are going to perform together for the first time!

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.670
So they are.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.910
And of course, it'll be produced by Kii-chan.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.120
I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:11.670
Me too!

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.610
Everything Kii-chan produces has something amazing about it.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.060
Go, go, go for it!

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.140
Fight, fight, fight!

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.020
Let's, let's, go, go!

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.890
Oh, oh, oh!

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.550
Compy, Compy! {ughhhhhhhhhhhhhhh}{fine by me}

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.770
If you don't analyze faster, Seira'll be here!

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:33.880
Did it come up with anything?

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.710
Yeah.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.030
To answer the question of how to make our first performance together

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.770
make as many people enjoy themselves as possible,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.090
it gave me this pro-pro-production plan! {aioerugthorgnoevnioneonm}

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.330
And the results are...

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.870
Ta-da!

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.950
We should create the choreography for the new song ourselves.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.920
Ourselves?

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.230
Yes!

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:57.930
We should make it the focus of our 
performance and make our fans happy!

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.620
Sounds like fun.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.380
I have no idea where to start, though.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.530
Apparently Seira-chan and Kii-chan are doing their own choreography for their new song.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.290
Really?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.750
We've never done any choreography before.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:47.540
Yeah.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.170
I did it once in America.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.170
One, two!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.030
Choreography for my friend Thomas.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.920
Oh, the orca.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:58.920
Yeah!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.250
What exactly did you do in America anyway?

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.860
All sorts of Aikatsu!

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:04.930
So that was Aikatsu?

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.930
I really want to know too, but...

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.810
Well, putting that aside...

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:12.620
How do you make choreography for idols?

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:14.290
Like this, like this!

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.400
Powa powa, puririn!

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.570
Powa, puririn!

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.590
Otome came up with this one!

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:27.490
Powa. Powa. Puririn!

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.900
Powa, puririn!

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.200
Well done!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.460
Shion-chan, you've totally assimilated, huh?

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.080
A-Assimilated?

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.960
I see you honeys are talking about choreography.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.590
Sounds interesting, yeah!

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.990
Johnny-sensei!

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.750
A pro choreographer!

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.760
What Arisugawa just did was a great piece of choreography. {how long has it been since Otome's last name was used anywhere}

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.430
However, the one who has done all of your choreography

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:56.940
was I, the pro dancer and choreography master!

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:04.250
Yes, I design top-level choreography to let you honeys shine your brightest!

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:09.140
Creating choreography from nothing can be likened to a fight with oneself.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:09.830
Powa...

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.070
Puririn!

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:11.990
Are you listening?!

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.210
This is my first time doing my own choreography.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.130
Me too.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:23.150
Making your own choreography and then memorizing it

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.260
sounds like a tough challenge.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.280
This analysis will help.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.870
Right, Compy?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.640
Magical Time.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.340
He says that this is the best song for us to use.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.650
Let's listen to it.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.940
Ok-ok-okay!

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.020
<i>It's a secret that every girl knows.</i>

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:56.740
<i>A loving heart is the key to a magical time.</i>

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:59.500
Isn't this a little too cute?

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:00.910
Not really.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.740
It's about what I imagined.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.510
Wh-Why did it pick such a cute song?

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.530
You're saying you think it goes against your image?

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.260
Yeah, I mean...

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:16.770
You said that the fact that I liked cats went against my image,

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:20.720
and isn't this pretty much the same thing?

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:21.900
Well, you see,

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:23.890
this is contrast.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.410
For idols, there are times when you need to keep your image

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:32.160
and times when going against your image creates something good.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.390
By contrasting the image you've built up so far,

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:39.810
you're showing the fans another wonderful side of yourself.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.670
I see.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.490
No wonder you're the producer.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:44.760
I approve.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:49.550
Because the song is so cute, you'll be able to show everyone another side of yourself.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.730
Alright!

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:52.930
Let's start thinking about the choreography!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:53.980
Yeah!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.430
Since it's our first time, let's find a teacher we can learn from.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.710
Can't we just go to one of the teachers from the idol course?

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.290
We <i>could</i> do that,

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.820
but since it's our first time performing together,

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:10.750
I want to find the best teacher I can!

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:12.820
Here it is!

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.780
Oh, this teacher?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.670
Yeah!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.940
Let's, let's go!

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:21.670
Okay!

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.280
Everyone, good work.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.420
Today's lesson is over.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.530
Thank you very much!

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.170
Good work!

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:30.930
{...}

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.740
Seira-honey and Kii-chan-honey.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.270
Welcome!

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.810
What are you doing here?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.310
We came here to see Johnny-sensei today.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.830
Nice to meet you, Johnny-sensei.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:45.520
Is it ok-ok-okay for us to be here?

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:48.570
Of course.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.400
It's ok-ok-okay!

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.840
Yeah!

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.210
You came here to learn about choreography?

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:01.400
Kii said the best person to learn choreography from was Starlight Academy's Johnny Gepp-sensei.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:02.750
Gepp?

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.250
No! He's Johnny <i>Bepp</i>-sensei!

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.550
Bepp!

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:14.930
Johnny-sensei is an amazing dancer who did choreography for the legendary idol group Masquerade,

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:21.430
as well as choreography for the super idol Kanzaki Mizuki-chan.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:22.990
Yeah.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:28.990
So before we draw up our own choreography, we want to learn from Johnny-sensei.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:33.550
I know we don't go to Starlight Academy...

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.320
Yeah!

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.450
You flatter me too much, Kii-chan-honey yeah!

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:43.220
Aikatsu Aikatsu Aikatsu Aikatsu...

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.220
He's spinning so fast...

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.750
He's going to drill a hole...

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:53.470
We at Starlight Academy are rivals of Kii-chan-honey's and Seira-honey's Dream Academy!

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:58.510
But we can still do some passionate Aikatsu together,

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.360
and get everyone pumped up, yeah!

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:02.290
Okay!

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:06.640
To that end, a lesson in Johnny-style choreography will begin!

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.310
Starmiya and company, join in too!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.400
Yes!

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:23.750
Recently, even regular schools have been doing choreography.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:25.960
They have dance classes.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:26.880
Yeah.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.500
However, we are professionals.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.880
I will teach you the four points necessary to be a pro.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.260
So long as you master these four points,

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.440
you'll be able to create awesome choreography, yeah!

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:40.510
And by the way,

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:45.520
this is the same Johnny-style 
choreography behind Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.620
This is a rare chance to learn the 
secrets behind his choreography!

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.190
It's all thanks to you two!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.890
Let's get started then!

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:59.720
Johnny's choreography lesson, point one!

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.320
The first thing to do

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:04.160
is to listen to the song while looking at the lyrics sheet.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.920
<i>It's a secret that every girl knows.</i>

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:16.930
<i>A loving heart is the key to a magical time.</i>

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:29.400
Honeys, do any images come to mind?

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:31.890
This is a cute and fun song.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:32.520
Yeah.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.280
With this line about a kaleidoscope, {lyric consistency}

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:39.300
it kinda feels like a world of toys.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.530
And like a jumping and floating feeling.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.900
And next!

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:48.080
Johnny's choreography lesson, point two!

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.460
Draw pictures next to the lyrics.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:52.210
Pictures?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.960
Draw?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:54.920
Yes.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.590
Like this.

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:00.430
Draw the poses that come to mind however you like.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.740
Or, for example, at this floating trampoline part,

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.430
you can draw a pretty "floaty" next to it.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.640
Anything goes.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:10.910
Kii.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:18.320
Just like you said, it does really
 feel like a world of toys and dolls.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.920
Yeah, somehow.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:20.890
I know, right?

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:23.150
Let's draw with that in mind.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:23.820
Okay.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.580
This is pretty fun.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.080
Floaty float.{...}

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.340
Bounce! And shake your butt, butt, butt, butt!{maybe I'll get back to this part later, fuck this}

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.240
Yeah!

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:41.620
Bang!

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:42.840
"Bang"?

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:45.850
Salute, salute, bounce-bounce-bounce!

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.220
That's so cute!

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.520
You can use it.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:51.150
Really?

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:56.570
And now, Johnny's choreography lesson, point three!

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:01.030
Move your body while looking at what you wrote on the lyrics sheet.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.700
Starmiya, that angle is impossible.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:09.330
Yeah?

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:19.760
Float, floooat... {eh}

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.050
Seira, Seira!

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:26.850
Wouldn't something like this be more "floaty"?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.040
Like this?

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.560
Yeah, just like that!

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:35.320
Everyone done? {Ichigo doesn't need water, apparently}{what a boss}

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:36.110
Yes!

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:37.560
Johnny-sensei, you're amazing!

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.550
Thanks to you, I think we can come up with some good choreography.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.570
Kii-chan-honey.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.910
The lesson's not over yet.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.080
There's still Johnny's choreography lesson, point four!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.250
That's right!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.790
The fourth and last point...

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.250
...is to think about who your supporters are.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:03.110
These are the people who make your dance the best it can be.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.200
Supporters?

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.760
Who are you talking about?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.800
That's for you to think over.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.720
Sometimes, one must take a hands-off approach to instruction

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.850
and allow the students to discover truths for themselves

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.370
so that it is burned into the back of their mind!

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:20.690
Okay?

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.490
I wonder what point four means.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:24.330
Let's think about it!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.090
Yeah!

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.580
Are you listening?

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.910
See ya, thanks!

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:30.940
Yeah!

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.550
I'm looking forward to seeing your performance!

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:34.900
Thank you!

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:40.040
We've got the moves of our choreography in order.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.080
Yeah, it's perfect.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.770
Now we just need to memorize this.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:44.800
Yeah!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:50.830
<i>Floating, floating on a trampoline of clouds.</i>

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:54.990
<i>I can jump all the way to the sky.</i>

00:13:54.990 --> 00:14:00.980
<i>Floating, floating in a weightless audition,</i>

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:05.780
<i>Let's go see whatever dreams we want.</i>

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.780
Finished!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.920
Let's look at the film.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:13.730
Yeah.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.420
Seira.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.940
It's a little... off, isn't it?

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:29.900
Yeah.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:30.800
But...

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.820
What is it?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.310
There was definitely something off.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.630
I just wonder what it is.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:47.280
We did the choreography perfectly.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.670
Ah, Seira-chan, Kii-chan!

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:51.910
Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.030
Recording?

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.760
No, we just have a meeting today.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:57.200
How did the choreography turn out?

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.210
Well, you see...

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:05.240
Wow!

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:06.320
It's so cute!

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.010
But I feel like something's off.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.850
And we don't know what it is.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.460
We had fun watching it.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:16.690
I think it was cute!

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.350
Yeah, she's right.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.450
I see.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:23.110
We were thinking that it didn't come out too great.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:26.110
Like it wasn't complete, or something.

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.070
Oh, I have an idea!

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:36.170
Why don't you just have fun out there?

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:37.620
Like, whee!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.620
Whee?

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.010
That could work.

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:43.080
Your choreography is meant to be cute, after all.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.500
And having fun is important.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.000
I see.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:52.720
And if you imagine that pictures are being taken of every move, you'll naturally be more precise. {accurate?}

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.720
Good one!

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.260
As expected of a model!

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.850
Aoi, what would you do?

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:02.710
If I had to choreograph something with Ichigo, Ran, and myself...

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:06.120
I'd probably just look at what Ichigo and Ran were doing.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:07.770
You're embarrassing me.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.410
If you look at each other, you'll be able to figure out how to make your poses better.

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:12.430
I see.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:13.530
She's right!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.070
One, two, three, four!

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.320
One, two, three, four!

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:19.550
One, two...

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:22.300
I understand when Seira shines the best.

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:23.040
Seira!

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:26.190
Try spinning your right hand around.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:27.590
Okay.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:30.260
One, two, three, four!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.760
One, two, three, four!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:36.540
I understand when Kii is the cutest.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.760
Yeah, that last one was great!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.960
The performance is almost here.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:49.780
It still feels like we haven't done enough.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.530
Compy, help!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.080
What's missing from our dance?

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:02.630
It's this!

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.730
Our dance moves are cramped way too tightly!

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:10.770
Then how can we make our movements more dynamic?

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.680
That's it! {no, you baka} {I don't know how that happened}

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.070
Once we do this training, we'll be perfect!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:18.800
Are we really going to do this?

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:36.410
Ai! Katsu!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:42.410
If we manage to guide a jumbo jet properly, our dance moves will naturally get grander!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.330
Ai! Katsu!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.340
Is this really Aikatsu?!

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:51.880
Dream Academy's Otoshiro Seira and Saegusa Kii!

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:54.620
At last, they perform together!

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:55.880
Seira!

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:01.390
Everyone's waiting for us.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.140
Yeah.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:06.390
It'd be a lie to say that there isn't anything I'm worried about in the dance,

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.520
but when I hear their voices...

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:12.770
Oh right! Choreography lesson, point four!

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:15.820
Think about who your supporters are.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.780
These are the people who make your dance the best it can be.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.240
Our supporters...

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.240
...are our fans?

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:28.340
Yeah! No doubt about it!

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:31.450
After all, it's their voices that are giving me energy now!

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.160
Both our courage and excitement are... {rghioonerogntuirhgiwehgief}

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.510
Ok-ok—

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.550
Okay!

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.510
Johnny-sensei.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:43.850
Thank you for guiding Seira and Kii.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:46.760
With the way they performed,

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.120
it looks like they've realized who their supporters are.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.550
By supporters, you mean the fans, right?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.120
Yay!

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.570
Our supporters were everybody!

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:57.370
Yeah!

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.750
Seira-chan!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:00.460
Hoshimiya Ichigo!

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:03.130
Your choreography was really cute!

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.380
Thanks!

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:06.890
Seira-chan, you were really cute too!

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:09.210
Yeah! New appeal, discovered!

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:10.770
Seira-chan, you're so cute!

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:14.750
I'm not used to being called cute...

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:16.140
But thanks.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:18.020
We can't let you beat us, though.

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:19.970
Yeah!

00:23:55.900 --> 00:23:57.790
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.030
How was our first choreography?

00:24:01.030 --> 00:24:04.460
It was fun matching our movements to the music.

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:07.040
And it was even more fun having everyone enjoy it!

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:09.920
Dance to increase fun!

00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:11.880
That's some yummy-looking chocolate!

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:15.580
There's a detective drama where they eat this chocolate when they get stuck.

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:16.450
Interesting-sounding!

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:18.010
Let's enter the audition together!

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:19.470
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:21.970
Wrap it up: Chocopop Sleuth. {isn't chocopop an actual thing? (wait, I think I'm thinking of chocolove}

00:24:21.970 --> 00:24:25.380
Always passionate, idol activities!
